# Cra keeps a page made ahead for the next tab that needs one (SparePages): the ~34 ms CEF spends
# making a page's window falls between clicks. The next tab takes it and loads its own address, and
# until then extensions don't see it: chrome.tabs.query and chrome.windows.getAll leave it out
# (spare-pages.patch). The fixture's button opens a page naming what it saw.
budget rss=900 stalls50=8
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/TabsQueryExtension
relaunch
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=one
wait 4
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=two
expect-log takes a spare page
wait 4
cra://debug?extensionAction=${TABS_QUERY_EXTENSION_ID}
wait 4
cra://debug?back=answer
expect-log back answer: selected=.*page\.html\?n=tabs-
reject-log back answer: selected=.*page\.html\?n=tabs-[0-9]+-blank-[1-9]
# Pane: a tab for one of Pane's own pages never takes the spare (PageEngines.nativeOwns), so Settings
# opens as its own page (SettingsPageBrowser), not as pane://settings in a Chromium spare.
pane://action/settings
wait 3
expect-log settings page read its state
pane://debug?settingsPageJS=location.href
expect-log settings page js: pane://settings
cra://debug?removeExtension=${TABS_QUERY_EXTENSION_ID}
wait 1
reject-log fault:
